WEBVTT

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.560
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.560
<i>Kagutsuchi steals books they believe
to be cursed tomes, then burns them.</i>

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.360
<i>While in pursuit of this group, the girl 
encounters a young man named Sagisawa Rui.</i>

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.000
<i>In his honest eyes is a wish to become a doctor 
out of admiration of his deceased parents.</i>

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.200
<i>However, a Kagutsuchi member 
has the same honest eyes.</i>

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.120
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her feelings.</i>

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.530
Nightingale Ball

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.530
-Nachtigal-

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.530
I'm back.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.160
Yes! I beat my record.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.470
Made it to nine places all by myself.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.790
Who are you?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:29.920
Huh?

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.920
What is a girl doing here?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.680
Oh... um, I just recently joined Fukurou.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.300
My name is Kuze Tsugumi.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.300
A woman in Fukurou? That's preposterous.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.060
Um, but...

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:51.060
Oh! Could it be that you recently 
joined Fukurou, as well?

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.630
Insolence! Of course I haven't done that!

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.800
How extremely unpleasant!

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.040
I'm sorry, you ran into him 
before I could introduce you.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.790
His name is Ukai Shougo-kun.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.960
He's the Prime Minister's son, who attempted 
suicide the same day as Hitaki-kun.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.490
He wrapped his tie around 
his own neck in his room.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:20.580
Luckily, one of the servants found 
him just before he asphyxiated.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.660
<i>He's just like Hitaki...</i>

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.260
Many people come and go from 
the Prime Minister's residence,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.710
making it unsuitable for 
healing emotional wounds.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.830
So a rush decision was made 
to take him in here.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.360
So that's why...

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.610
Being in a new and unfamiliar environment 
must be unsettling for him.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.740
Ukai-kun!

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.750
Could you turn that down a bit?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.130
Ukai-kun!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.340
We can hear your record player out here!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.620
The little lord's really at it.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.940
And so soon after moving in here...

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.390
They can probably hear it 
even out in the street.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.640
Ukai-kun!

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.140
I'm coming in!

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.160
How dare you?! Don't just 
come in my room! Hey!

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.300
Damn you!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.540
That's enough, both of you.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.050
Hayato, calm down.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.290
Shougo-kun, this is a communal living 
space, and as such, there are rules.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.140
You are expected to follow
them while you're here.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.160
It wasn't my decision to come here.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.040
But the reality is that you <i>are</i> here.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.760
Young master!

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.550
Ah, excuse me.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.480
What is the matter, young master?

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.430
Don't call me that!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:53.150
Kijitani, I've been through hell because 
you took so long to come back!

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.670
My apologies, young master.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.860
I told you to stop calling me that!

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.730
I will be imposing on you as of today.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.840
My name is Kijitani Arata.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.070
It's a pleasure to meet you all.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.080
Nice to meet you. Nice to meet you. 
Thank you in advance.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:15.840
It's surprising that his 
servant is with him, too.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.900
It seems he isn't your typical housemate.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.210
In other words, kind of like you.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.210
Is that so?

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.720
I'd like to make it work somehow, 
but the outlook is grim.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:29.850
Um...

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.410
I think Ukai-san is still 
having a rough time after

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.730
what happened with the cursed tome.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.610
My brother is still in the hospital,

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.230
so I think Ukai-san will need more time, too.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.260
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:48.240
We'll just have to be patient with Ukai-kun.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.040
Yes, have patience.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.240
<i>I'm sure he'll be fine.</i>

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.420
<i>Right. I'll start by greeting him properly.</i>

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:06.620
Awaken, awaken, sparrows in your nest...

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.640
Good morning!

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.340
So you're one of the servants?

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.190
No, we take turns cleaning.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.700
I'm a member of Fukurou.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.750
There's no way a woman could 
handle that kind of work.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.350
What kind of look is that?

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:29.500
You ought to look cuter and more girlish.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.780
You're being rude.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.160
Excuse me?

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.540
I'm still new and not 
very experienced yet,

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.000
but there are many women 
working hard at their jobs.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.980
That includes Tokimiya-san!

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.550
B-Be quiet!

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.900
I don't want to hear that from an 
uppity, frivolous girl like you!

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.840
How extremely unpleasant!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.850
I overdid it...

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.850
What happened to being patient with him?

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.900
I'm sorry. I couldn't help it.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.610
I'm just teasing you.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:07.490
Trying to be too delicate with someone 
like that isn't a good idea, either.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.110
I think you did the right thing.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.980
I hope so.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.010
What is it? What's wrong?

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.620
I've been waiting for you.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.630
Let's talk inside.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.630
Someone jumped to their death?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:37.520
Yes, from a building near 
Tokyo station late last night.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.300
The police are keeping 
a lid on any information,

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.940
but apparently a Japanese-style 
book was lying next to him.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.270
A cursed tome?

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:50.300
The man who jumped was a member of the 
House of Representatives, Kamoike Eisaku.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.780
A politician?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.280
Also, according to another bookstore owner,

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:57.410
he was coming back from Nachtigal.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.910
Nachtigal?

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:04.710
I see... So you heard, too.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.230
You already knew about this?

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.050
We even hurried back to tell you.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:12.550
He told me.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.450
Hey, Hayato.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:15.860
Senpai!

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:16.930
Senpai?

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.180
This is Yoshikiri-san, a journalist 
for the Imperial Capital Newspaper.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.710
The Imperial Capital Newspaper?

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.650
He's Hayato's senpai from college,

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.810
and we exchange various information.

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.820
I finally get to meet you, Kuze Tsugumi-san.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.390
One of my colleagues told me

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:38.270
that she had a friend who's 
working hard at Fukurou.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.880
Are you referring to Koruri-chan?

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.580
Yes.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:46.710
I knew it had to be her! 
It's nice to meet you.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.090
Likewise.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.960
Now, getting back on topic...

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.140
Actually, the incident with the politician, 
last night's jumper, isn't the only one

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.320
thought to be related to a cursed tome.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.660
Did you hear about the death 
of a House of Lords member

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.300
named Abi Kiyomaru, about a month ago?

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.500
Didn't he die from some disease?

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:12.100
The official announcement was that he had 
a heart attack in his bedroom at home.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:17.240
However, according to the servants, there 
was a Japanese-style book at his bedside.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.740
Does that mean it was a cursed tome?

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:27.000
I don't know, but his wife 
is a regular at Nachtigal.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.100
Intriguing, isn't it?

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.130
I was surprised to hear it, too.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:36.100
So, this Nachtigal... is it in Ginza?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:39.420
A truly sleepless, gloriously resplendent,

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.920
high-class, members-only dance hall.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:47.520
And the den of the Karasu 
organization, or so we suspect.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.840
Karasu? You mean the group 
intentionally making cursed tomes?

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:58.410
The cursed tomes they make are supposedly 
being sold at Nachtigal's black auction.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.240
Why haven't you investigated 
or arrested them?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.870
Have you heard of Shiginuma Takashi?

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.160
Of course.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.880
He's the head of the famous Shiginuma Group.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.170
I haven't met him, though.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.760
He's also the owner of Nachtigal.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.930
And we suspect that he might be
the mastermind behind Karasu.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:20.800
It can't be!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.260
He has close ties to political 
and business circles

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.290
and has fearsome skill when it 
comes to destroying evidence.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.410
Without some conclusive evidence, 
there's nothing we can do.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:34.190
You can't do anything even 
when people are dying?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:37.620
That's precisely why we're 
investigating every day,

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:41.200
and why we're always exchanging 
information with Yoshikiri-san like this.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.130
I'm sorry...

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.190
My lady, do you know how to waltz?

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:53.460
Ah, yes, more or less.

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:55.500
That's perfect.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.080
Shougo-kun received an invitation 
to a party at Nachtigal.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.980
It's a Western-style event where 
men and women attend together.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:04.520
I'd like you to accompany him as his escort.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:05.350
Huh?

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:09.430
This will be the first chance 
we've had to infiltrate Nachtigal.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.520
W-Wait... This won't work!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.740
I'm certain he'll refuse.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:16.930
Why?

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.160
Because he finds me extremely unpleasant.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.120
This is extremely unpleasant!

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:29.140
This may be a request from you, 
Tokimiya-san, but I won't do it!

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:31.530
There's no way I would waltz with that girl!

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:32.760
But Kuze is...

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:35.000
An absolutely detestable girl.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.510
She keeps showing up wherever 
I am and speaking out of turn.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:41.560
She's vulgar, uncivilized, and repulsive!

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:42.920
Young master...

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.630
Don't call me that!

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:45.680
But...

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.880
A-Anyway, I refuse!

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:02.780
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:06.480
<i>I can't seem to get any closer to him at all.</i>

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:22.470
H-How dare you?! I can't believe you'd even wait to ambush me <i>here</i>!

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:26.250
I wasn't waiting for you! 
This is the women's bath!

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.680
Women

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.810
Y-You saw... saw me n-naked...

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:36.440
I didn't! I didn't see anything!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:52.080
<i>That was a total shock...</i>

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:58.960
What are you doing here?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.710
I'm not waiting for you.
It's just a coincidence.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.840
They all have been.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.850
I'm sorry about earlier. 
It wasn't on purpose.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.970
I-I know that.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.420
I didn't see anything, okay?!

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.980
I'm aware of that, too.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:22.560
Kijitani told me that you're 
a daughter of the Kuze family.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:23.460
I am.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:24.440
Why?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:28.490
Why is the daughter of a noble 
family living in a place like this?

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:33.810
I came here not too long ago, 
but I really enjoy it now.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.300
Enjoy it?

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:38.500
It's cheap, the walls are thin, 
and the rooms are small.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.880
They even make you clean. 
It's the worst place ever.

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:44.620
Those are all the reasons I enjoy it.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:46.510
I have freedom here.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:48.340
Freedom?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.760
Without Gramps here to protect me,

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.760
I can make my own decisions.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:58.470
I have my own job, and I receive 
a wage that I can spend as I wish.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.500
Also, I like this job.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:04.780
I've always loved books, after all.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:09.530
But the people here are just 
a bunch of vulgar idiots.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.790
No, they're all wonderful people.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.190
Communal living is fun.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:22.540
Which is why I hope we can all get 
along better with you, too, Ukai-san.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.650
Wha... D-Don't be ridiculous!

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.240
...wouldn't mind.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.050
Huh?

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:34.430
I'm saying I guess I wouldn't 
mind taking you to the ball.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.430
Thank you!

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.500
This is extremely unpleasant!

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.190
The knife is for self-defense.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.200
Don't go thinking you need to do anything 
special on the day of the party.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.700
What kind of guests come 
and go, the black auction,

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.640
whether or not there are discussions 
about the cursed tomes—

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:00.270
that's all you need to pay attention to.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:01.210
Yes, ma'am.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:04.230
Don't create any dangerous 
situations, no matter what.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.960
Understood.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:09.720
That said, well done getting
Ukai-kun to accept.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:13.780
I think that Ukai-san is 
actually a very kind person.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:15.660
Yes, that's true.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.480
Now, then, we have to order your dress.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.260
Dress?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.920
Nice! It's really gorgeous!

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:31.740
Agreed.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.720
It makes me want to whisk you away myself.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:38.500
It looks very nice on you.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.930
Th-Thank you...

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:43.250
This is completely unacceptable.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.500
It's obvious you're not accustomed 
to wearing such clothing.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:52.630
You definitely look at home in 
a well-tailored suit, Ukai-san.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.080
Shut up.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.000
Anyway, conduct yourself 
in a dignified manner

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.090
so that you don't look unsightly beside me.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:03.650
Okay!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.620
Let's go.

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:07.570
Ah, wait for me! We'll be off now.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.910
That kid really isn't very honest.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.040
We will be arriving shortly.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.290
<i>This is Nachtigal?</i>

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:31.040
<i>It's so brilliant and beautiful!</i>

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:36.320
<i>But horrible things are going on 
in the shadows of this beauty.</i>

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.360
Don't just stand there spacing out. This way.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.810
Ah, Shougo-kun!

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:49.600
Shiginuma-san, Shouko-san.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.300
Thank you so much for inviting me.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:56.460
What a rare pleasure to have you join us.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:59.610
And you've brought such a 
lovely young lady with you.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:03.540
I-I was asked to bring her along.
It wasn't my choice.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.580
She's the daughter of my mother's friend.

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.080
My!

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.340
This is Kuze-san.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.960
Nice to meet you. My name is Kuze Tsugumi.

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:15.470
Welcome to Nachtigal.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:17.820
I'm the owner, Shiginuma Takashi.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.260
It's a pleasure to meet you, 
adorable little birdie.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:27.730
I am his wife, Shouko.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.980
Thank you for having me.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.480
<i>The scent of roses?</i>

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.220
The night is young. Please relax
and enjoy yourselves.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:37.900
We will.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.520
Oh? Shougo-kun?

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.000
What a relief you seem to be well.

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:51.000
I'm glad to see that you 
are also well, Owase-san.

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:55.510
I heard about a disturbance 
regarding a suspicious book.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:58.510
<i>Who is this man?</i>

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:00.960
Like father, like son.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.180
What a troublesome man 
the Prime Minister is.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:06.520
Pacifism and disarmament are weaknesses.

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.020
One misstep, and he becomes a traitor.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:12.040
I would ask that you refrain 
from speaking ill of my father.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.320
Goodness, my apologies.

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:16.780
I'll take my leave.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.680
Ukai-san...

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.480
It's hard to breathe in here.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:23.640
I'm going outside to get some air.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:24.790
I'll go, too.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.890
You wait here.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:27.690
But...

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:29.250
I told you to wait.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:39.320
<i>It certainly is difficult to breathe in here...</i>

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:50.430
<i>Sasagoi-san? And... who is that?</i>

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:56.450
<i>What is Sasagoi-san doing here?</i>

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:04.350
Why are you making that face?

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:06.960
Do you really dislike 
dancing with me that much?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.240
I'm sorry! That's not it at all.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.500
Don't apologize.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.920
It's not like I want to be 
dancing with you, either.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.340
I hate these kinds of things.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:21.320
I'm not very good with them, either.

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:26.540
I see... But the occasional waltz isn't so bad.

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.390
This is the first time I've felt that way.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.350
Yes!

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:40.070
I see... So Sasagoi was there.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:43.490
Yes, and there was a man with a cane, as well.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:47.760
He was shorter than Sasagoi-san, 
and his hair was tied in back.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:51.370
Mozuyama?

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:57.480
That man might be Professor Mozuyama 
from the Imperial Capital University.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:59.880
There have been some shady rumors about him.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.890
All right, we'll try looking into him.

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.040
You did well, Kuze.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:09.250
No, I just happened to see them.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:13.380
I think your ability to draw out 
coincidences like that is a talent, too.

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:23.530
U-Um, this is just a coincidence...

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.410
It's not. I knew you would 
come here, so I was waiting.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:32.440
I heard about your brother 
from Ozaki and the others.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:36.420
They told me it happened on the same day.

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:37.790
It did.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:43.840
Then you became able to see the auras 
of cursed tomes and came here.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.100
That's right.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:52.930
I'm sorry. I called you frivolous 
without knowing your circumstances.

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.870
No, it's okay.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.170
So, where is your brother now?

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:01.450
He's still hospitalized at the Imperial 
Capital University Hospital,

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:03.800
but I'll be able to see him soon.

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:06.700
I see. I'm glad.

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:09.360
Me, too. Thank you.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.420
Stop it.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.120
Your manner of speaking is too stiff.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.550
Ukai-san?

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:18.330
Stop that, too.

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.840
Call me Shougo.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:21.930
What?

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:23.340
Just say it.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:27.090
Shougo-san?

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.140
You can leave off the "san."

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.240
But...

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:35.100
Sh-Shougo...

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:36.850
Good.

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:39.740
That's all I wanted.

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:45.360
Apparently, I'm on cleaning duty tomorrow.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:49.980
You will teach me how to clean, Tsugumi.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:52.990
Okay, Shougo!

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:09.890
<b>Romantic Lilac Night</b>

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:21.910
<i>Yo, Kuina here.</i>

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:36.430
Chapter 5:  "Akatsuki Evening -Lilac-"

00:23:21.910 --> 00:23:24.570
<i>You seem to have gotten used 
to your job at Fukurou.</i>

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:26.840
<i>Though I liked seeing you hapless and naïve...</i>

00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:31.960
<i>Which reminds me, apparently there 
have been some disturbing incidents.</i>

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:34.800
<i>Always be careful, princess.</i>

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:38.480
<i>If you'd like, I'll keep you 
company all night long.</i>
